I think wishless ascensions are a combination between luck, patience and 
skill. Luck doesn't have to enter in to it, but if you have it, you'll 
need less patience. Skill would also be needed, since if you don't have 
that, you'll need a *lot* of patience to make up for all those magic 
markers you could have wished for. So the skill is sometimes doing 
without AC -60, or speed boots, or a helm of brilliance. I think it's 
more fun, but opinions differ.

Genoless isn't that hard, I think, once you know how to deal with 
(master) mind flayers and liches. All are very survivable with an 
ascendable character.

Also, I think it's more a question of what *you* like. Sure, a naked 
foodless weaponless petless illiterate atheist pacifist gets you 
respect, but the game has to be fun for you in the first place. If you 
find wishless genoless too easy, try something different, like atheist, 
illiterate, or both. They introduce different challenges into the game.

